{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence","id":1551710,"title":"Absent and influence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-16T03:24:25-07:00","id":1551710,"title":"Absent and influence","content":"Ok, the rules for Absent are great, I love the idea of palyign a ghost (possibly even more than playing an Ephemeral Cultist in the Mummy rules for playable Ephemerals).<br /> <br /> How and ever, apart from all the fun things you can do (join a mummy cult and get a mission which makes following the Mummy's orders giving the Impassioned Shade condition, or become a Familiar to some Mage character...) there are lots of things that a character in a Geist game can do.<br /> <br /> Gain effective rank by donning the Krewe's Regalia of Eminence (does this change the ban/bane to the equivalent of a rank 3 entity? Or is it not an issue since rank 2 and 3 ghosts have the same kinds or bans&amp;names).<br /> <br /> Resolve anchors and gain protection from essence bleed - but losing their influence, and thus being more detached from the world (for a player character would this be an endgame scenario, rather than allowing the character to continue in play with no anchors? And thus no influence).<br /> <br /> Gain rank by working on their memory (it is clear there are two main ways which Ghost gain rank, by being infused with the energies of the Underworld - death masks/drinking from the rivers - Or by working with memories of themselves, rank 1 to 2 when resolving the Actor condition with the help of the Break the Cycle haunt, or consuming a doppleganger of yourself - which presumably has memories from a different time in the ghost's life). However the rules assume you must drink from the Waters of the Underworld *only*, and that becoming a Geist makes a character unplayable (which is fine, but if I want a rank 3-5 playable ghost for high levels play, not so much fun).<br /> <br /> So I'm going to assume that (by the book) an Absent character with a Krewe (with the Regalia to make it rank 3) has to buy up all the numina/manifestations/attributes/influence it needs to act as an effective rank 3 entity. And further that resolving Anchors is a double sided blade (losing the ability to use influence without replacing them or getting sanctity of merits type benefits, while also being protected from Essence bleed, and being able to roam freely... You still need to spend 1 essence to remain active for a day - which might be easy to find if you take over a slaughter house and eat the rank 0 Barghest which are created there daily... Or a rubbish yard and consuming castoffs).<br /> <br /> Ideally you want your Krewe to be something of an Ancestory worshiping cult and make it up of people who remember you when you were alive. With a weekly ritual aimed at boosting your essence (or at least ritual sacrifice of some objects/animals to allow the cast off/Barghest being consumed for essence).<br /> <br /> Family members, friends, ideally a few of them trained as necromancers... Does a Krewe require any Bound? Or is it just easier to form one? (Maybe a Krewe whose bound have all passed on...) yeah, this would be becoming a NPC cult/antagonist...<br /> <br /> At which point, apart from the obvious (consuming Dopplegangers, Shades or goetia of the same person, and literal magic) is there anything a Ghost can do to increase their power further - without becoming a Geist/Reaper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T05:15:53-07:00","id":1551714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence#post1551710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gain effective rank by donning the Krewe's Regalia of Eminence (does this change the ban/bane to the equivalent of a rank 3 entity? Or is it not an issue since rank 2 and 3 ghosts have the same kinds or bans&amp;names).</div> </div> </div> </div>The statblocks of the example Reapers in the book make it clear the Ban and Bane only change if the ghost's Rank changes to one in a different band of Ban and Bane severity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resolve anchors and gain protection from essence bleed - but losing their influence, and thus being more detached from the world (for a player character would this be an endgame scenario, rather than allowing the character to continue in play with no anchors? And thus no influence). </div> </div> </div>This is a non-issue \u2014 see &quot;Sanctity of Influences&quot; in the section on Influences on Page 190. Ghosts who belong to krewes might take a cue from spirits who belong to packs and reassign their Influences to benefit their krewe, provided they have an understanding about not forcing them to Pass On.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gain rank by working on their memory (it is clear there are two main ways which Ghost gain rank, by being infused with the energies of the Underworld - death masks/drinking from the rivers - Or by working with memories of themselves, rank 1 to 2 when resolving the Actor condition with the help of the Break the Cycle haunt, or consuming a doppleganger of yourself - which presumably has memories from a different time in the ghost's life). However the rules assume you must drink from the Waters of the Underworld *only*, and that becoming a Geist makes a character unplayable (which is fine, but if I want a rank 3-5 playable ghost for high levels play, not so much fun). </div> </div> </div>Memoria only allows a ghost to go from Rank 1 to 2 for the same reason that it doesn't give a character with no traumatic Conditions superpowers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I'm going to assume that (by the book) an Absent character with a Krewe (with the Regalia to make it rank 3) has to buy up all the numina/manifestations/attributes/influence it needs to act as an effective rank 3 entity. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you need to spend at least 19 Experiences to get from the maximum stats for a Rank 2 ghost to the minimum stats for a Rank 3 ghost, which still requires you to drink from a River per Rank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ideally you want your Krewe to be something of an Ancestory worshiping cult and make it up of people who remember you when you were alive. With a weekly ritual aimed at boosting your essence (or at least ritual sacrifice of some objects/animals to allow the cast off/Barghest being consumed for essence). </div> </div> </div>If a ghost belongs to a krewe it can gain Essence in place of Willpower from participating in actions that collectively fulfill its Virtue and/or Creed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Family members, friends, ideally a few of them trained as necromancers... Does a Krewe require any Bound? Or is it just easier to form one? (Maybe a Krewe whose bound have all passed on...) yeah, this would be becoming a NPC cult/antagonist... </div> </div> </div>The Krewe Binding Ceremony does not require a Bound ritualist to perform, nor does an active krewe require its leadership to have the unique partial deathproofing of the Bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At which point, apart from the obvious (consuming Dopplegangers, Shades or goetia of the same person, and literal magic) is there anything a Ghost can do to increase their power further - without becoming a Geist/Reaper? </div> </div> </div>Unique magical bullshit dependent upon your game and setting, as well as more conventional stuff like the Quicken Ghost spell from Mage or the third Tier of the Words of Dead Dominion Utterance from Mummy, same as how the Rank 5 haunted smog from the &quot;Bad Air Day&quot; Story Seed exists without any more mechanics than &quot;this coalescence happens within a week if the weather doesn't change.&quot; There are deliberately no mechanics in Geist that are unambiguously designed for a ghost to consistently gain access to massive supernatural power without forsaking their humanity or compromising their morals by drinking from the Rivers or taking up a Deathmask; the +1 Rank from the Regalia of Eminence is as close as it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T05:39:43-07:00","id":1551715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence?p=1551714#post1551714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The statblocks of the example Reapers in the book make it clear the Ban and Bane only change if the ghost's Rank changes to one in a different band of Ban and Bane severity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a non-issue \u2014 see &quot;Sanctity of Influences&quot; in the section on Influences on Page 190. Ghosts who belong to krewes might take a cue from spirits who belong to packs and reassign their Influences to benefit their krewe, provided they have an understanding about not forcing them to Pass On. </div> </div> </div>That is interesting. I was imagining a really bad reading of the rules where you give up Manifestations to gain numina and give up those numina to gain influence over your anchors, and then resolve all your anchors (this being for a PC ghost) and then reassigned the XP to buy up new powers, but Sanctity of Influence is a clear rule which I had missed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Memoria only allows a ghost to go from Rank 1 to 2 for the same reason that it doesn't give a character with no traumatic Conditions superpowers. </div> </div> </div>It is the only other means of gaining rank, even given that it is only for rank 1 ghosts. (Apart from Death related) And the haunt is called Memoria, like memory has significance... Though that feels like it is more about making a ghost whole, by breaking them from a memory - it feels like adding to their whole self and making them more like the person they once were. AKA not twisted them with the power of the Underworld...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, you need to spend at least 19 Experiences to get from the maximum stats for a Rank 2 ghost to the minimum stats for a Rank 3 ghost, which still requires you to drink from a River per Rank. </div> </div> </div>Then I assume Absent can't gain rank by consuming their dopplegangers per your reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a ghost belongs to a krewe it can gain Essence in place of Willpower from participating in actions that collectively fulfill its Virtue and/or Creed. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I had forgotten that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Krewe Binding Ceremony does not require a Bound ritualist to perform, nor does an active krewe require its leadership to have the unique partial deathproofing of the Bargain. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so while that Ceremony is innate to Sin-eaters, ghosts learning it and binding themselves to a Krewe would be fairly unusual... Also liable to pissing off some Reapers if a Krewe of ghost does manage to carve out a little Niche for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unique magical bullshit dependent upon your game and setting, as well as more conventional stuff like the Quicken Ghost spell from Mage or the third Tier of the Words of Dead Dominion Utterance from Mummy, same as how the Rank 5 haunted smog from the &quot;Bad Air Day&quot; Story Seed exists without any more mechanics than &quot;this coalescence happens within a week if the weather doesn't change.&quot; There are deliberately no mechanics in Geist that are unambiguously designed for a ghost to consistently gain access to massive supernatural power without forsaking their humanity or compromising their morals by drinking from the Rivers or taking up a Deathmask; the +1 Rank from the Regalia of Eminence is as close as it gets. </div> </div> </div>The other method mentioned in the book is a NPC necromancer who has consumed so much necrotic power that he returns as a rank 4/5 Geist (per Necromancer Blues, pg 273). Which may qualify as &quot;magical BS&quot; but is definitely in the &quot;forsaking your humanity&quot; side of things.<br /> <br /> Or the Death/Underworld aspect of easy routes to power.<br /> <br /> I would tend to assume that, apart from Regalia, and Memoria helping rank 1 ghosts increase to rank 2. The main method of gaining rank would be merging with yourself. Requiring multiple different sides of yourself to become one.<br /> <br /> But my question was apart from the things already discussed above, am I missing anything that a ghost can do to increase their power (not rank).<br /> <br /> Like the ceremonies section on Innate Sin-eater ceremonies says &quot;other characters can buy them normally&quot; but the Absent character advancement stuff doesn't include an XP cost for learning ceremonies...<br /> <br /> I think I would have assumed only the living can learn and perform ceremonies, I doubt, for example a ghost could learn a rite from a spirit the same way Werewolves (or other pack members) can. Unless I am wrong and a ghost can join a pack and learn the same Rites any other pack members could.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T06:09:20-07:00","id":1551716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence?p=1551715#post1551715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the only other means of gaining rank, even given that it is only for rank 1 ghosts. (Apart from Death related) And the haunt is called Memoria, like memory has significance... Though that feels like it is more about making a ghost whole, by breaking them from a memory - it feels like adding to their whole self and making them more like the person they once were. AKA not twisted them with the power of the Underworld...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's technically also completely resolving the Remembrance, but that requires becoming a geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I assume Absent can't gain rank by consuming their dopplegangers per your reading of the rules. </div> </div> </div>My reading of the setting is generally that the mechanics for ghosts gaining Rank by consuming Doppelg\u00e4ngers of the same person, combined with the mechanics for ghostly starting Rank, assumes that Doppelg\u00e4ngers of the same person at Rank 2 are not common enough for one to reach higher than Rank 3 without abnormal circumstances, and that the rules for the Absent are written with the assumption that characters using an alternative means of Essence to supplement their Anchors in the living world are disinclined toward an act that is one of the few repeatable breaking points they can undergo outside the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the ceremonies section on Innate Sin-eater ceremonies says &quot;other characters can buy them normally&quot; but the Absent character advancement stuff doesn't include an XP cost for learning ceremonies... </div> </div> </div>You get them for free from krewe membership scaled with your Mystery Cult Initiation and the non-krewe-based cost is included in the more conventional chart on Page 77. Presumably it's not included on the Absent character advancement chart because the Absent are, barring the Dead Meat Merit, markedly more constrained in their ability to get the necessary components to perform a Ceremony without assistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I would have assumed only the living can learn and perform ceremonies, I doubt, for example a ghost could learn a rite from a spirit the same way Werewolves (or other pack members) can. Unless I am wrong and a ghost can join a pack and learn the same Rites any other pack members could. </div> </div> </div>The Forge Anchor Ceremony specifically includes in its Requirements that the ritualist must be one of the Bound or one of the living, which directly implies this is not a universal requirement of Ceremonies. Rites are not the same thing as Ceremonies, given that the former require a connection to the Shadow that even living normal humans can't emulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-16-2025, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T07:00:41-07:00","id":1551718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence?p=1551716#post1551716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's technically also completely resolving the Remembrance, but that requires becoming a geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am ignoring the ways Geists gain rank, but competing their Remembrance is also in the &quot;memory&quot; category of growth for Geists.<br /> <br /> That said, I am pretty sure Geists are explicitly non-playable entities for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My reading of the setting is generally that the mechanics for ghosts gaining Rank by consuming Doppelg\u00e4ngers of the same person, combined with the mechanics for ghostly starting Rank, assumes that Doppelg\u00e4ngers of the same person at Rank 2 are not common enough for one to reach higher than Rank 3 without abnormal circumstances, and that the rules for the Absent are written with the assumption that characters using an alternative means of Essence to supplement their Anchors in the living world are disinclined toward an act that is one of the few repeatable breaking points they can undergo outside the Underworld. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you mention the rank 2 doppleganger. Since a ghost of whatever rank can consume any rank of doppleganger to gain rank or the doppleganger rules, iirc.<br /> <br /> The rarebess of Dopplegangers is the issue (and the fact that they are each other's banes) - but it also seems to be a bit of a default for them to destroy each other:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist 2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiously, when two ghosts formed from the same person touch, they merge, the weaker of the two destroyed and consumed as essence by the stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they touch, doesn't seem to imply one of them consciously engaging in Ectophagia... Even if mechanically that seems to be required, two ghost from the same person being each other's banes, makes touching not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't seem like the more pleasant wording 'they merge'...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get them for free from krewe membership scaled with your Mystery Cult Initiation and the non-krewe-based cost is included in the more conventional chart on Page 77. Presumably it's not included on the Absent character advancement chart because the Absent are, barring the Dead Meat Merit, markedly more constrained in their ability to get the necessary components to perform a Ceremony without assistance.<br /> <br /> The Forge Anchor Ceremony specifically includes in its Requirements that the ritualist must be one of the Bound or one of the living, which directly implies this is not a universal requirement of Ceremonies. Rites are not the same thing as Ceremonies, given that the former require a connection to the Shadow that even living normal humans can't emulate. </div> </div> </div>Ok, that is a fair point as regards Ceremonies.<br /> <br /> Rites i am assuming would require joining a Pack, and I'm not sure how likely it is that a group of werewolves would allow a ghost (though possibly the ghost if a fallen wolf-blooded might be an exception) to join a pack.<br /> <br /> There are rumour of packs without werewolves, just humans and spirits (possibly shadow Occultist) in one of the antagonist books for WtF. So I'm just imaging how a Krewe could learn a and teach necromancy, or a ghost could join a Shadow-Occultist Pack or Forsaken Pack, and consume spirit essence /otherwise make a connection to the Shadow (not that this is likely to gain them any rank, but other powers potentially).<br /> <br /> I do have a one-shot story in my head somewhere which revolves around a group of teenage friends who end up going into the hedge (after one of their group gets kidnapped by the Fae) and they all promised to help each other - thus becoming fae-touched. But almost every character ends up either dead (Absent), a Hedge Ghost, or otherwise with some nasty ending... But I can imagine player Ghosts entering the Hedge and search for Icons (aka memories) and holding them dear (or using them as Memories in the standard Absent Memory usage way). Or there is a Rank 4 example ghost (Echo) created by God-Machine Shenanigans is the Demon antagonists...<br /> <br /> Generally I'm trying to think of things which *any* ghost could do. Obviously any ghost *could* resolve all their anchors... Actually managing it is a different matter.<br /> <br /> But if they can learn and lead ceremonies that is fairly strong (rather than being used as fuel by Necromancers).<br /> <br /> A mage could capture their soul just before death and graft is back into the ghost to see what happens, but that is more of a Mage story than a ghost one... (Or Make multiple dopplegangers for them to merge into).<br /> <br /> Mummy has Ephemeral Cultists, though the rules for Absent seem more comprehensive, and I'm still confused by the mechanics of how Mummy works.<br /> <br /> Some ghost end up in the astral just by virtue of (maybe) believing they are supposed to be in that astral realm of death...but beyond that there is no evidence the average ghost can meet astral versions of themselves (or temenotic versions) without something else intervening - though again, I would argue the kind of intermingling of self to gain power would make sense... (The version of you in the Temenos is based largely on other people's perspectives, so may be a bad thing...).<br /> <br /> Whatever Shades are, maybe ghosts and shades of the same person can exist aswell. And maybe they are different parts of the five-fold soul.<br /> <br /> Vampires might leave a ghost behind when embraced, which is probably not a good thing... But possessing/fettering/claiming the vampiric body of that was once your own seems like something not every ghost can do...<br /> <br /> What am I forgetting? Hunter probably has some cool stuff, Deviant is all out of the norm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T08:07:53-07:00","id":1551719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence?p=1551718#post1551718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you mention the rank 2 doppleganger. Since a ghost of whatever rank can consume any rank of doppleganger to gain rank or the doppleganger rules, iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mention it because a character who never forms a ghost above Integrity 6 needs to form one extra ghost (and/or successful assistance from a master of the Memoria) in order to produce a Doppelg\u00e4nger capable of reaching the same level as one who creates a ghost with a starting Rank of 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are rumour of packs without werewolves, just humans and spirits (possibly shadow Occultist) in one of the antagonist books for WtF. </div> </div> </div>Shadow Occultists can learn and perform Pack Rites without a pack via their connection to their spiritual patrons, and otherwise at least an appropriate form of Wolf-Blooded Tell is needed to perform a Pack Rite if the pack doesn't have the Moon's Grace Merit that specifically can only be taken by packs with no werewolves in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummy has Ephemeral Cultists, though the rules for Absent seem more comprehensive, and I'm still confused by the mechanics of how Mummy works. </div> </div> </div>The base Ephemeral Cultists mechanics are that any type of ephemeral cultist can hold Pillars through the Rite of Investment and treats gatherings of their mummy's cult as Open, with all other effects being particular to the type of entity; ghost cultists aren't forced into the Underworld and thus presumably treat their initiation into a Scorpion Cult as an Anchor in only that sense, still needing actual Anchors and/or living memory and/or ectophagia to gain Essence on top of requiring the relevant Conditions to Manifest.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, it is a thematically enforced point of ghosts in Geist that without very unusual circumstances, you need to step outside of humanity to get greater preternatural power than a handful of Numina, a PFR Attribute spread, and a Trait cap of 7. If you want Big Magic Powers as a ghost, your options amount to drinking deep of necromantic power, getting a supernatural patron, and/or engaging with an unpublished plot device (or homebrew Merits) in or beyond the same general vein as &quot;dedicated supernatural or supernatural-adjacent organizations can tweak the rules of magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T08:30:33-07:00","id":1551720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1551710-absent-and-influence?p=1551719#post1551719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mention it because a character who never forms a ghost above Integrity 6 needs to form one extra ghost (and/or successful assistance from a master of the Memoria) in order to produce a Doppelg\u00e4nger capable of reaching the same level as one who creates a ghost with a starting Rank of 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.<br /> <br /> I guess i was confused. 1) dopplegangers can be rank 0 as parts of a body. Thus more easily absorbed (infact I can imagine a conflict between a human with a ghostly arm and their doppleganger who may find consuming said arm to be handy... Pun intended).. but most dopplegangers determine their rank &quot;the usual&quot; way. Which is based on the integrity at the point of their creation.<br /> <br /> As such, a tortured soul could start with high enough integrity, and create an initial Rank 2 doppleganger, but be variously transformed by the removal of limbs or other nefarious means and end up a shattered (lower integrity) character only able to produce rank 1 ghosts...<br /> <br /> I see the process as making a new person, ie leaving behind the old one. Obviously this is verging on Deviant creation in the true output.<br /> <br /> Obsessed Mage, or mad scientist, some twisted Uglan created trying to prove something, or what ever unhinged antagonist would try it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadow Occultists can learn and perform Pack Rites without a pack via their connection to their spiritual patrons, and otherwise at least an appropriate form of Wolf-Blooded Tell is needed to perform a Pack Rite if the pack doesn't have the Moon's Grace Merit that specifically can only be taken by packs with no werewolves in them. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I don't think Absent can become Shadow Occultists, even if they can join a pack.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a Werewolf pack who wolf-blooded sibling dies, leaves a ghost who stay in the pack, and becomes either connected to the Totem, or forced to take over when the Pack's totem is destroyed (or the ghost-sibling eats the Totem, in an act of ectophagia/hunt).<br /> <br /> Any pack having a Ghost as their Totem instead of a Spirit would be interesting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The base Ephemeral Cultists mechanics are that any type of ephemeral cultist can hold Pillars through the Rite of Investment and treats gatherings of their mummy's cult as Open, with all other effects being particular to the type of entity; ghost cultists aren't forced into the Underworld and thus presumably treat their initiation into a Scorpion Cult as an Anchor in only that sense, still needing actual Anchors and/or living memory and/or ectophagia to gain Essence on top of requiring the relevant Conditions to Manifest. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Broadly speaking, it is a thematically enforced point of ghosts in Geist that without very unusual circumstances, you need to step outside of humanity to get greater preternatural power than a handful of Numina, a PFR Attribute spread, and a Trait cap of 7. If you want Big Magic Powers as a ghost, your options amount to drinking deep of necromantic power, getting a supernatural patron, and/or engaging with an unpublished plot device (or homebrew Merits) in or beyond the same general vein as &quot;dedicated supernatural or supernatural-adjacent organizations can tweak the rules of magic.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Very unusual circumstances are on thing. Like that Rank 4/5 Geist on death example.<br /> <br /> But I'm really asking about other sources of power not rank.<br /> <br /> Scorpion Cult, Pack rites, Ceremonies, are all fairly interesting character options. Especially forming a Krewe and perhaps an Ancestory worship cult, along with ritual scarifice to create castoffs/Barghest.<br /> <br /> Learning new Numina from Spirits/Angels/Goetia or travelling to the Underworld/Astral to discover lost pieces of knowledge/themselves... Make for some potentially good stories. Especially if it is just a character who your average Bound/Mage/Werewolf happens to come across on their own journey...<br /> <br /> I think the God-Machine would love to play with some ghosts some times...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}